(text "Universal LV pinout docs/modular/slot_pinout_LV.csv; engine pinout\ncards/engine/engine_slot_pinout.csv. Slot ID straps: slot n = ID n-1, 0 = GND,\n1 = open (card pull-up); IDP makes ID0..2+IDP odd. ID_WP is high (protected);\nPB6 -> AO3400A pulls it low for factory/calibration writes (all LV slots +\nengine). Expanders on I2C2: 0x20 P0 EN_N / P1 PWR_FAULT_N (eFuse FLT#/PGOOD +\nTPS2553 FAULT), 0x21 P0 INT_N / P1 ARM_N, 0x22 P0 CARD_FAULT_N, P10\nENG_PRESENT_N, P11 BANK_EN, P12 BANK_FAULT_N, P13 BANK_OVL_ROOM (out), P14\nBANK_OVL_N (in). Slot ANA_OUT -> 1k -> U109 (EN = PE13 SLOT_ANA_EN, 100k pull-\ndown).\nPass 6 M3: J48 a13/c13 = ENG_3V3_SAFE through U160 TPS2553 (210k: 110-150 mA,\nauto-retry, FAULT -> ENG_PWR_FAULT_N on 0x22 P15); J48 a12/c12 = ENG_VBAT_P\nthrough U161 TPS16630 eFuse (30k: 0.54-0.66 A vs <= 0.13 A load, 1 us short\ncut, auto-retry, FLT#/PGOOD -> ENG_PWR_FAULT_N). A cracked cap or bent pin on\nthe engine card no longer collapses +3V3_SAFE or blows F1." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 703.58 22.86 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "296145e8-df45-4c3d-b08d-39a1040b7a43"))
(embedded_fonts no))
